 ### Inputs and Outputs
-*   **Inputs:** Ground truth images $I(\mathbf{o}, \boldsymbol{\omega}_o)$, camera poses, scene geometry (implicit or explicit), and initial parameters for the Zip-NeRF cache, physically-based model, environment map, and fast cache.
-*   **Outputs:** Optimized Zip-NeRF radiance cache parameters, physically-based model parameters, environment map, and fast cache parameters.
+**Inputs:**
+*   Dataset of multi-view images (e.g., TensoIR-synthetic, Open Illumination).
+*   Camera poses and intrinsics.
+*   Initial Zip-NeRF structure (sparse hash grid + MLP) and Fast Cache structure (low-res hash grid + small MLP).
+*   Physically-based material model parameters $\Phi$.
+*   Environment map parameters.
+
+**Outputs:**
+*   Optimized Zip-NeRF radiance cache.
+*   Optimized Fast Cache.
+*   Optimized material parameters $\Phi$.
+*   Optimized environment map.
 
 ### Data Structures
-*   **Zip-NeRF Radiance Cache:** A sparse voxel grid structure (as defined in [Acceleration and Sparse Structures](11405-acceleration-and-sparse-structures.md)) storing radiance features.
-*   **Fast Cache:** A lightweight hash grid and small MLP predicting incident radiance.
-*   **Physically-Based Model:** Parameters defining surface reflectance (e.g., BRDF/BTDF coefficients).
-*   **Environment Map:** Parameters defining the incident lighting field.
+*   **Zip-NeRF Cache:** A sparse hash grid storing features, decoded by an MLP to predict radiance. Accessed via spatial constraints defined in [Acceleration and Sparse Structures](11405-acceleration-and-sparse-structures.md).
+*   **Fast Cache:** A lightweight hash grid and small MLP predicting incoming radiance $L_{fast}$ [S1].
+*   **Occlusion-aware Importance Sampler:** Samples directions for cache evaluation.
 
